            <title>2.1.0</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 22:16:27 +0300</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>2.1.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Snapline 2.1.0</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Backgrounds</b> — the annotation editor gains a Background stage: wrap a capture in a gradient or solid-color backdrop with padding, rounded corners, and a drop shadow before sharing. Ten gradient presets or any solid color; the result is baked into Copy, Done, Save to File, and drag-out alike.</li>
  <li>Background settings stay editable. Reopen a capture from History and the backdrop, padding, corners, and shadow are yours to change &mdash; the original pixels are untouched underneath.</li>
  <li>Snapline remembers your last Background configuration and offers it on the next capture you annotate. Off by default; Tall Captures are excluded.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
